mudi (0.4.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix terminal color schemes (Theme 1-10 and others) missing from the
    settings page in CI-built packages: COLORSCHEMES_DIR was baked with
    the default /usr/local prefix while the deb/rpm install to /usr, and
    the relocatable fallback concatenated the app dir and the "../share"
    macro without a separator, producing a path that never exists. CI now
    configures with CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr and the fallback inserts
    the slash, so installed and portable layouts both resolve the data
    directory. Affects all GitHub-release debs since v0.3.0; local deepin
    builds were unaffected (system terminalwidget reads its own data dir).

 -- re2zero <re2zero@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0800

mudi (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the CI-built Linux binaries failing on systems with an older
    libstdc++ ("GLIBCXX_3.4.32 not found"): release builds now link
    libstdc++ and libgcc statically, removing the libstdc++ version
    requirement entirely. glibc stays dynamic.

 -- re2zero <re2zero@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:10:00 +0800

mudi (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the CI-built deb refusing to install on deepin: the vendored
    terminalwidget data (color schemes, keyboard layouts) now lives in
    /usr/share/mudi/terminalwidget6 instead of the system
    /usr/share/terminalwidget6 tree owned by deepin-terminal — no more
    dpkg file conflict, and the relocatable fallback finds the new
    location for portable installs.

 -- re2zero <re2zero@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0800

