mudi (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Redesign the settings dialog in DTK style: group cards, pill
    switches, semantic status banners, theme swatch cards and rounded
    controls; palette-aware so it follows light/dark on every platform.
  * New settings features: search, restore defaults, a do-not-disturb
    window for agent notifications, rotating file logs with an
    open-folder entry, and a GitHub feedback link.
  * Harden the update pipeline (M9): background checks throttled to
    once per 6h, conditional requests (ETag/304) that spare the GitHub
    rate limit, a static gh-pages index checked before the API, and
    deb-managed installs kept under the package manager's control
    (portable builds self-update from the banner).

 -- re2zero <re2zero@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 25 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0800

mudi (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Close the herdr server lifecycle loop (M7): a low-frequency
    `herdr status` probe tracks the running server, and after a herdr
    update the app now offers a guided restart — destructive-action
    confirmation, stop, and an automatic relaunch that reattaches the
    client in place. Protocol mismatches and pending restarts surface
    as a banner and in the herdr settings page.
  * Name agents by their project: caps, tray entries and notifications
    read "project (agent)" so same-named agents stay distinguishable.
  * Remove the in-window agent status strip: it duplicated the herdr
    client sidebar; window-side monitoring stays with herdr, MuDi
    watches from outside the window (notifications + tray).

 -- re2zero <re2zero@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800

mudi (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the project to MuDi (牧笛): binary, desktop entry, icon,
    settings store and release assets are now "mudi"; an existing
    deepin-herdr settings store is imported on first run.
  * Fix the frontend failing to enter herdr when relaunched while the
    server is still running: the client was spawned before the window
    was laid out and exited on a zero-sized terminal grid; the spawn
    is now deferred until after show().
  * Add in-app updater (mirror racing, SHA-256 verification) with a
    progress banner and a paginated settings dialog.
  * Add agent state desktop notifications (AgentMonitor).
  * Use DTK only on deepin/UOS and a generic Qt window shell elsewhere;
    vendor terminalwidget sources for all-platform builds.
  * Auto-restart the herdr server after stop and attach reliably, with
    lifecycle banners and a fallback plain shell.
  * Add CI build matrix (linux x86_64/aarch64, macOS) with optional
    libchardet.
  * Notifications navigate to the agent pane: clicking the body or the
    "View" action raises the window and runs `herdr agent focus`.
  * System tray presence with agent summary tooltip, blocked-agent
    menu shortcuts and an optional close-to-tray mode; quitting from
    the tray goes through a confirmation with an explicit choice to
    stop the herdr server.

 -- re2zero <yangwu@uniontech.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0800

